WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.080
Star-Lord has quickly risen to being one of
Marvel's most popular heroes, thanks to his

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.039
role in Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:12.540
But just a few years ago, barely anyone — even
comic book fans — knew who he was.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:16.820
His newer fans might be surprised to discover
that he's kind of a galactic jerk, even though

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:21.390
the Marvel Cinematic Universe made him look
more like Han Solo than Boba Fett.

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.920
Here's the dark side of Star-Lord you never
knew about.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.210
He brainwashed the Guardians

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:31.320
The modern Guardians consist of some of the
universe's best warriors, but also some of

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.070
its most notorious loners.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:36.120
How did Quill convince everyone to join the
team?

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:41.510
He had another team member, Mantis, brainwash
all of them to think it was a good idea.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:45.490
Even worse, he didn't even try asking first,
he just went straight to brainwashing.

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:49.740
Forcing people to do something they normally
wouldn't do is like the textbook definition

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.309
of being a villain, so good job Star-Lord.

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:53.450
You creep.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:55.920
That time he rescued Thanos

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.950
As the big bad guy of the Marvel Universe,
Thanos once killed half of all life — not

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:04.670
just on Earth, but literally everywhere, simply
because he could.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:08.140
He also has a crush on the female embodiment
of death.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.780
Not this one...or this one...but this one.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:12.780
Everyone has a type.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:17.750
During Marvel's Thanos Imperative story, Star-Lord
and Nova sacrifice themselves to help trap

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:21.760
Thanos in another universe, because that's
the heroic thing to do.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:26.990
But while Nova makes good on the self-sacrifice,
Star-Lord finds a way out — and brings Thanos

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:27.990
with him.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:33.130
Star-Lord's truce with Thanos brings the universe's
worst villain back into action, and that just

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:36.060
seems like another creepy villain thing to
do.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.220
He caused Annihilation Conquest

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:43.329
In the Marvel comic universe, the first Annihilation
War basically broke the galaxy, but it never

00:01:43.329 --> 00:01:46.020
would have happened if it wasn't for Star-Lord.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:50.040
He had invited a group of Space Knights to
come update the Kree homeworld's security

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.570
systems, but the Space Knights had already
been infected by the Phalanx.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:58.009
For those who don't know, the Phalanx are
basically Marvel's version of The Borg.

00:01:58.009 --> 00:02:01.869
And at the time, they'd actually been taken
over by Ultron.

00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:06.620
One thing leads to another, and the entire
universe is almost assimilated into the Phalanx

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:10.609
consciousness, all because Star-Lord thought
the Space Knights were cool.

00:02:10.609 --> 00:02:11.609
Which they aren't.

00:02:11.609 --> 00:02:13.099
Just look at this guy!

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:15.650
He's like a heroic trash can or something.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.090
No thanks.

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:18.430
He endangered Earth

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:21.510
Earth: it's primitive and weak.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:26.269
Different alien species are always trying
to invade it, and the planet always just barely

00:02:26.269 --> 00:02:27.269
survives.

00:02:27.269 --> 00:02:31.620
That being the case, it's not a good idea
to put the planet in extra danger, but Star-Lord

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:32.969
didn't read the memo.

00:02:32.969 --> 00:02:37.599
In the comics, his father, the ruler of the
planet Spartax, basically puts a target on

00:02:37.599 --> 00:02:42.719
the Earth, unless Peter returns to the Spartax
Empire as a member of the royal family.

00:02:42.719 --> 00:02:44.319
That doesn't sound so bad, does it?

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:49.209
But of course, in true Star-Lord fashion,
he doesn't just immediately slip into a life

00:02:49.209 --> 00:02:51.010
of royal intergalactic luxury.

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:53.980
Instead, he puts all of his friends and family
in danger.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:57.920
To be fair, Peter's dad J'Son isn't exactly
the nicest guy.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.180
Eventually, Star-Lord helps remove his father
from the throne, but then he just leaves,

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:05.849
so it surprises him when Spartax elects him
to be their next leader.

00:03:05.849 --> 00:03:10.010
Since he's the heir to the throne and also
the empire's big hero, this should have been

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:11.010
obvious.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:14.969
But instead of fulfilling his duties, Quill
tries to just abandon his people.

00:03:14.969 --> 00:03:17.349
That life of luxury must be a real heavy burden.

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:19.860
And when he finally did take the throne later
on?

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.790
He did such a bad job that his people ousted
him.

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:23.900
Oh, well.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:24.999
He was a lounge singer

00:03:24.999 --> 00:03:29.779
When all of reality crashes together during
Marvel's Secret Wars, a small contingent of

00:03:29.779 --> 00:03:34.059
heroes survive the end of the world on a lifeboat
built by Reed Richards.

00:03:34.059 --> 00:03:37.779
When they land on the patchwork planet of
Battleworld, Star-Lord finds himself in an

00:03:37.779 --> 00:03:40.319
alternate version of Manhattan.

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:43.949
Instead of getting back into the hero game,
he works as a lounge singer, until he meets

00:03:43.949 --> 00:03:46.409
up with an alternate version of Kitty Pryde.

00:03:46.409 --> 00:03:50.139
He finds his way back to the resistance to
help lead the charge against God Doom, the

00:03:50.139 --> 00:03:54.829
ruler of Battleworld, but he'd probably still
be singing if he'd never run into an actual

00:03:54.829 --> 00:03:55.829
hero.

00:03:55.829 --> 00:03:56.870
Speaking of which...

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:58.379
He's insanely jealous

00:03:58.379 --> 00:04:02.749
Peter Quill and Kitty Pryde were the "it"
couple of the Marvel Comics universe for a

00:04:02.749 --> 00:04:06.809
bit, but their relationship took a turn for
the worse when Star-Lord decided to step up

00:04:06.809 --> 00:04:11.290
and become the leader of Spartax, prompting
Kitty to take up his old mantle as the new

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:12.629
Star-Lord.

00:04:12.629 --> 00:04:16.870
Peter didn't like having another, more effective
Star-Lord kicking around the galaxy, and the

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:19.829
two had a fairly messy breakup before reconciling.

00:04:19.829 --> 00:04:22.770
Maturity has never been one of Quill's strong
suits...

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.260
“What are you doing?”

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:29.590
“I’m distracting you, ya big turd blossom!”

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:30.639
Thanks for watching!

00:04:30.639 --> 00:04:33.590
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:35.950
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

